Player movement in 1st and 3rd person views was inverted - W moved backward, S moved forward. The input Z-axis signs were reversed in the control mapping.

## Changes

Corrected the Z-axis input direction for W/S keys in `Player.tsx`:

```typescript
// Before (inverted)
if (keysPressed.has('KeyW') || keysPressed.has('ArrowUp')) inputZ -= 1;
if (keysPressed.has('KeyS') || keysPressed.has('ArrowDown')) inputZ += 1;

// After (correct)
if (keysPressed.has('KeyW') || keysPressed.has('ArrowUp')) inputZ += 1;
if (keysPressed.has('KeyS') || keysPressed.has('ArrowDown')) inputZ -= 1;
```

The camera-relative movement calculation on lines 80-81 transforms these inputs using the forward vector, so positive `inputZ` now correctly moves forward along camera direction.

