The file list table allows sorting by all columns. "New Name" column should be non-sortable since it displays computed preview values that change based on operations.

## Changes

**State Tracking**
- Added `lastSortColumn` and `lastSortOrder` members to track last valid sort state
- Initialized to column 0 (Original Name), ascending order

**Sort Interception**
- Connected to `QHeaderView::sortIndicatorChanged` signal
- When column 1 clicked: capture current state and restore via queued invocation
- When other columns clicked: update tracking state normally

```cpp
connect(header, &QHeaderView::sortIndicatorChanged, this, 
        [this](int logicalIndex, Qt::SortOrder order) {
    if (logicalIndex == 1) {
        // Capture to avoid race conditions
        int column = this->lastSortColumn;
        Qt::SortOrder sortOrder = this->lastSortOrder;
        QMetaObject::invokeMethod(this, [this, column, sortOrder]() {
            this->treeWidget->sortByColumn(column, sortOrder);
        }, Qt::QueuedConnection);
    } else {
        this->lastSortColumn = logicalIndex;
        this->lastSortOrder = order;
    }
});
```

Value capture prevents race conditions where sort state could change between signal emission and queued lambda execution.

