Automated fix for ts-execute-service

The fix adds an input validation check to ensure the input is not null and matches a valid number format before attempting to parse it, thus preventing the NumberFormatException.

Related Issue: #151

## Changes
```diff
--- a/ts-execute-service/ExecuteService.java
+++ b/ts-execute-service/ExecuteService.java
@@ -1,10 +1,12 @@
 package com.ts.execute.service;

 import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;

 @Service
 public class ExecuteService {

-    public Response executeRequest(String input) {
+    public Response executeRequest(String input) {
+        if (input == null || !input.matches("\d+")) {
+            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid input: must be a number");
         }
         try {
             int number = Integer.parseInt(input);
             // Process the num
         } catch (NumberFormatException e) {
             return new Response("ERROR", "Invalid number format: " + e.getMessage());
         }
     }
 }
```

The `UpdateLastEditedDate` method was splitting on `\n` and rejoining with `\n`, causing mixed line endings when input used CRLF (`\r\n`) - existing lines retained `\r`, while replaced/inserted lines lost it.

## Changes

- Detect original newline style (CRLF vs LF) by checking for `\r\n` presence
- Split on both `\r\n` and `\n` to avoid leaving dangling `\r` characters
- Join using detected newline style to maintain consistency

```csharp
// Detect the newline style used in the content (CRLF or LF)
var newline = content.Contains("\r\n") ? "\r\n" : "\n";

var lines = content.Split(new[] { "\r\n", "\n" }, StringSplitOptions.None);
// ... processing ...
return string.Join(newline, lines);
```

Added tests verifying CRLF/LF preservation for both replacement and insertion scenarios.

