The `_fetchYearFile` fallback in `viewModal.js` lacked in-flight request deduplication. Rapid date range toggles before fetch completion triggered multiple concurrent requests for the same year file.

**Changes**

- Added `_viewYearFetchPromises` Map to track in-flight requests per year
- Check Map before initiating fetch; return shared promise if request already in-flight
- Clean up Map entry in `.finally()` after fetch completes (success or failure)

**Implementation**

Mirrors the `historicalFetchPromises` pattern from `spot.js`:

```javascript
// Check cache → check in-flight → create & store promise
if (_viewYearCache.has(year)) return Promise.resolve(_viewYearCache.get(year));

if (_viewYearFetchPromises.has(year)) {
  return _viewYearFetchPromises.get(year);
}

const promise = fetch(localUrl)
  .then(...)
  .catch(...)
  .finally(() => _viewYearFetchPromises.delete(year));

_viewYearFetchPromises.set(year, promise);
return promise;
```

The fallback path now deduplicates concurrent requests identically to the primary `spot.js` implementation.

