<summary>Original prompt</summary>

> ## Bug Fix: Button Flip Toggle Disabling Fly Feature
> 
> ### Issue:
> When the "Button Flip" toggle is clicked, the fly double-tap feature gets disabled and prevents the "Fly Down" button from working. The button flip state is being incorrectly reset.
> 
> ### Root Cause:
> In `PlayerOptionsController.cs`, the `ToggleButtonFlip()` method (lines 168-186) has a logic error:
> - It checks `if (!inVR || !_doubleTapEnabled)` and calls `ResetButtonFlipState()`
> - This causes the button flip to ALWAYS be reset to false when the toggle is pressed, defeating the purpose of the toggle
> - It should only reset if NOT in VR, not when double-tap is disabled
> 
> ### Fix Required:
> 
> **PlayerOptionsController.cs - ToggleButtonFlip() method:**
> Change the logic from:
> ```csharp
> if (!inVR || !_doubleTapEnabled)
> {
>     ResetButtonFlipState();
>     return;
> }
> ```
> 
> To:
> ```csharp
> if (!inVR)
> {
>     // Only reset if not in VR
>     ResetButtonFlipState();
>     return;
> }
> 
> // If we get here, we're in VR. Only allow toggling if double-tap is enabled
> if (!_doubleTapEnabled)
> {
>     // Don't toggle, but also don't reset - just return silently
>     return;
> }
> ```
> 
> This way:
> - If NOT in VR: Reset flip state (safety check)
> - If in VR but double-tap is OFF: Don't toggle (silent fail)
> - If in VR AND double-tap is ON: Allow the toggle to work properly


</details>



